. LESSON 1 GETTING STARTED
. In these examples color 1 is teal, not red. $L1 says which of the
. palette's 256 colors color 1 shows (lesson 7); 29 is teal, and
. $L1=1 makes it red again.
$L1=29
. A line that starts with a period is a comment, and is skipped.
.
. PRINT does arithmetic. % picks a number at random between two others.
PRINT 5
PRINT 5*5
PRINT 5*2+2
PRINT 5*(2+2)
PRINT (5*2)+3
PRINT 100/3

PRINT 1%5

PRINT A=10%100

A=10%100

A = 10%100

PRINT A

PRINT PRINT 10

PRINT PRINT PRINT 10

PRINT(10)
PRINT(PRINT(PRINT(10)))

PRINT 10,20,30
PRINT(10,20,30)

PRINT(PRINT(10)+PRINT(5))

HELP

PRINT HELP()

. BOX XCENTER,YCENTER,XSIZE,YSIZE,COLORMODE draws a filled rectangle.
BOX 0,0,300,200,3
BOX 75,0,20,100,2
BOX -75,0,20,100,1
BOX 0,0,200,10,0

BOX 0,0,320,200,3;POINT 100,20,0

CLEAR
BOX 0,0,100,100,3
BOX 0,0,50,50,2
POINT 0,0,1

. POINT with no colormode reads the screen: 1 2 3 and -1 (off-screen)
PRINT POI(0,0),POI(0,1),POI(30,-30),POI(200,200)

. THE ANIMATION. CONFETTI draws one box, at a random place, of a random
. size and a random colormode (0 is black), and SKIP 0 runs its line
. again, for ever. A macro is a name given to lines in brackets, as
. lesson 2 shows. Press ESC to stop it.
CONFETTI=[BOX -160%159,-100%100,4%40,4%40,0%4;SKIP 0]
CONFETTI
